WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.960
Okay, so a release notes template puts the upgrade decision before the details.

2
00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:09.467
My summary at the top says who has to act and what to do,

3
00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:12.533
including when rollback stops being safe.

4
00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:14.773
In my SDK example,

5
00:00:15.073 --> 00:00:18.813
the summary tells Python users they can ignore the release,

6
00:00:18.813 --> 00:00:20.967
so they stop after one line.

7
00:00:20.967 --> 00:00:25.807
Then each breaking change gets a migration step and a check that proves it worked,

8
00:00:25.807 --> 00:00:28.267
plus a deadline with a calendar date.

9
00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:33.607
Before publishing, my checker fails a note with a missing rollback line or a vague deadline,

10
00:00:33.607 --> 00:00:36.707
so in CI it can't merge until it passes.
